/* xim-import.js - "Copy your XIM settings in": the PURE half, window.ZSXIM.
 *
 * A player who owns an XIM (MATRIX, APEX or NEXUS) types the numbers from
 * their XIM app into a screen laid out like XIM's Aim Settings
 * (xim-import-screen.js, the `ximimport` screen). This file holds everything
 * that screen decides, with no DOM, so dashboard/tools/test-xim-import.js
 * runs it in Node:
 *
 *   defaults(mt)          the form, filled in from this config's own numbers
 *                         (so a field left alone changes nothing) and XIM's
 *                         published starting values where it has them
 *   validate(form)        every visible number checked against its range,
 *                         one plain sentence per bad field
 *   preview(form, ctx)    every XIM field -> what it becomes here, with an
 *                         honest label (Same / Close / Not available) and the
 *                         exact config writes it makes; nothing else is ever
 *                         written
 *   applyWrites(doc, w)   makes those writes on a config document and returns
 *                         what they replaced, so undo(doc, list) puts it back
 *   looksLikeShareCode(t) true when pasted text is an XIM share code
 *   fromShareCode(t, mt)  a pasted code's numbers in the form, with a report
 *                         of what was filled, not copied and not read
 *   applyPreset(form, id) a typical starting point into the form
 *
 * The mapping is docs/GPC-XIM-IMPORT-ASSESSMENT.md section 2.4, ROUTE A ONLY
 * (the player types their own numbers). See docs/XIM-IMPORT.md.
 *
 * Since D189 and D191 the Core has real homes for three XIM fields that
 * used to land nowhere, and they are written there now:
 *   - Smoothing STANDARD | CLASSIC (D191): Standard's Precision / Response /
 *     Easing on the 0-100% scale the Aim page shows (Precision = smoothing /
 *     0.95), Classic's Smooth / Decay / Synch as classicSmooth / Decay /
 *     Synch (and the ads* twins), with smoothingStyle naming which;
 *   - QUANTIZATION, Magnitude and Angle, per stance (D189, section 0x0026):
 *     quantMagnitude / quantAngle (and adsQuant*), 0..1 for XIM's 0..100;
 *   - the CURVE (D189): our editor is XIM's kind now (2 to 16 handles), so
 *     the handles copy across as they are, stored the way the editor stores
 *     them (seven numbers or { v: 2, h, s }).
 * An adapter without them (an EXO: PRODUCTS.exo.lacks 'classicSmoothing',
 * 'aimXim') keeps the old answer, "Not available", and writes nothing:
 * preview(form, { hides }) is told which.
 *
 * SHARE CODES (route B, docs/XIM-SHARE-CODE.md): fromShareCode() hands a
 * pasted code to xim-share-code.js (ZSXIMCODE), which reads the few mouse-aim
 * fields the public samples confirm, and puts them INTO THE FORM. Nothing is
 * applied from a code: the player sees the form and the preview, with its
 * labels, and taps Apply. A number this app cannot hold is reported and left
 * alone, never guessed; the code's text is not kept. Nothing here talks to
 * XIM's servers or Config Cloud.
 *
 * TYPICAL STARTING POINTS (PRESETS, applyPreset) and the screenshot guide
 * (SCREENSHOT_HELP) come from docs/XIM-PUBLIC-CONFIGS.md: typical community
 * values, said to be exactly that, never XIM's official data.
 *
 * Wording (D76): "copy your XIM settings in", never "XIM compatible", and no
 * XIM logos anywhere.
 *
 * ES5 ONLY, like every file phone.html loads (docs/DESIGN.md).
 */
(function (root) {
  'use strict';

  /* ── XIM's ranges ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     XIM's own guide (https://guide.xim.tech/Aim-Settings/, read 2026-10-02)
     names every field below and gives units, but publishes NO numeric range
     for any of them. The only numbers it states are Synch's ("8=Default,
     16=Common, 32=Slow, 0=Off") and the Quantization starting point ("set
     Magnitude to 25 and Angle to 25"). So:
       - where a field lands on one of OUR fields, the range is what that
         field can hold (the app's own range, else profiles/schema.py), so
         every number accepted here can be applied;
       - Classic smoothing and Quantization have homes since D191 / D189,
         so their ranges are those homes' ranges: Smooth 0-100, Decay 0-20,
         Synch 0-64 ms (the Aim page's Classic steppers), Magnitude and
         Angle 0-100% (the Aim page's Quantization).
